※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4577

※ A record is its fields, so a value of one is a value for each of them.  There
※ is no default to fall back on and nothing that would be right to leave behind:
※ a field left out would be storage holding whatever was there, which is the
※ thing this language does not have.
※
※ C fills such a field with zero, which is the half of the designated
※ initializer not taken here: zero is a value like any other and a program that
※ meant it can write it.

type Point = x : u32 ; y : u32

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let p : Point = Point(.x ← 1u32)
    if p.x = 1u32: 0u6 else: 1u6
